From c7af4e18d19f7d114872e0473793288dc3262538 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:14:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MSI M3: per-device routing (xHCI MSI-X live, AHCI gains MSI)

Both controllers already had exactly one place computing their
interrupt level; each becomes the router.  xHCI: xhci_intx_update now
branches on the M1-programmed state -- MSI-X enabled forces the INTx
pin silent (PCI rule) and sends one message from vector-table entry 0
on the level's rising edge, re-armed when the guest's ack lowers the
level; a masked interval (per-vector or Function Mask) delivers on
the unmask write itself (router call sites added to table-MMIO writes
and to the cfg-write canonicalisation).  Disabled, the pin path is
byte-identical to X5.

AHCI gains the MSI capability in the shape measured from two ICH
lspci dumps ("[80] MSI: Count=1/1 Maskable- 64bit-"): ahci_pci_seed
plants it at cfg 0x80 on both controllers (Status.Cap + pointer 0x80,
one message, 32-bit address; a PM cap exists on silicon but belongs
to PM_PLAN, not invented here).  cfg_write folds Enable/Address/Data
into ahci_t with RO re-assertion, and its S5 intx_update routes by
the same edge rule.

Vectors: test-xhci v_msix_route walks enable -> message -> held-level
exactly-once -> ack re-arm -> per-vector mask/unmask -> Function
Mask/unmask -> disable/pin-return through the real LAPIC arbitration;
test_ahci test_msi_line drives real command completions through both
transports against a locally seeded pci_dev.  NCs: xHCI engine at M2
-> 5 failures in the route group (its fallback expectations keep
passing, by design); AHCI route branch stubbed -> pin asserts where a
message was due.  Gates: make test, make test-sanitize, both SeaBIOS
ISO lanes green; no lane anywhere enables MSI, so historical
receipts are untouched by construction.
